# SHELVED PR-41 tooling: locally generated .LVM set is scratch, never
# committed (regenerable via tools/mv_convert.py; derived bytes must not
# enter history). Full record: NEXT_STEPS.md PR-41 (SHELVED).
movies/

# Reference gameplay captures (YouTube, PR-111): the videos, their
# .info.json and their .description are copyrighted - never in git.
# The ids, URLs and the re-download commands live in HANDOFF.md
# section 3 ("Reference captures"); .mp4 frames cut from them stay in
# /tmp/opencode/ as always.
reference/video/

# Agent skills (SKILL.md trees for OpenCode/Claude) are local tooling:
# verify-docs P5 (tools/doc_census.py) inventories every TRACKED .md and
# fails outside the closed docs set, so these stay untracked on purpose.
.opencode/
